<title>UK: BASKETBALL-MEN'S EUROLEAGUE RESULTS.</title>
<headline>BASKETBALL-MEN'S EUROLEAGUE RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of men's EuroLeague</p>
<p>basketball matches on Thursday:</p>
<p>Group A</p>
<p>In Athens: Panionios (Greece) 69 Maccabi Tel Aviv (Israel)</p>
<p>74 (halftime 34-44)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Panionios - Fanis Christodoulou 10, Keath Gadlin 9</p>
<p>Maccabi - Back Johnson 12, Velimir Radovic 9</p>
<p>Attendance: 3,000</p>
<p>Group A</p>
<p>In Limoges: CSP Limoges (France) 84 Ulkerspor Istanbul</p>
<p>(Turkey) 80 (54-41)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Limoges - Yann Bonato 26, Vern Fleming 13, Gerald Glass 11</p>
<p>Ulkerspor - Kevin Rankin 21, Orhun Ene 18, Daniel Godfread</p>
<p>11</p>
<p>Attendance: 5,000</p>
<p>Group A</p>
<p>In Milan:</p>
<p>Stefanel Milano 87 CSKA Moscow 74 (49-45)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Stefanel - Flavio Portaluppi 21, Gregor Fucka 16, Anthony</p>
<p>Bowie 15</p>
<p>CSKA - Serguei Bazarevitch 21, Marcus Webb 11, Valery</p>
<p>Daineko 11</p>
<p>Attendance: 2,700</p>
<p>Group B</p>
<p>In Madrid:</p>
<p>Estudiantes (Spain) 94 Charleroi (Belgium) 72 (44-32)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Estudiantes - Harper Williams 18, Chadler Thompson 17, Juan</p>
<p>Aisa 16 </p>
<p>Charleroi - Adam Wojcik 25, Ron Ellis 20</p>
<p>Group B</p>
<p>In Athens:</p>
<p>Olympiakos (Greece) 62 Cibona Zagreb (Croatia) 61 (36-32)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Olympiakos - Willy Anderson 19, Panayotis Fasoulas 13,</p>
<p>Dragan Tarlac 11</p>
<p>Cibona - Damir Moulaomerovic 20, Zdravko Radoulovic 7, Davor</p>
<p>Marcelic 7</p>
<p>Attendance: 7,000 </p>
<p>Group D</p>
<p>In Pau: </p>
<p>Pau-Orthez (France) 80 Efes Pilsen Istanbul (Turkey) 78</p>
<p>(34-37)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Pau - Antoine Rigaudeau 36, Fabien Dubos 18, Thierry Gadou</p>
<p>11</p>
<p>Efes - Petar Naumoski 32, Huseyn Besoc 10, Meurat</p>
<p>Evlyialoglu 10</p>
<p>Attendance: 6,000</p>
<p>Group D</p>
<p>In Bologna</p>
<p>Kinder Bologna (Italy) 100 Partizan Belgrade (Yugoslavia) 83</p>
<p>(45-43)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Bologna - Komazec 35, Savic 20, Prelevic 18</p>
<p>Belgrade - Beric 26, Tomasevic 21, Cubrilo 11</p>
<p>Attendance: 5,600</p>
</text>
